# The modules the in-body comment ban holds (scripts/comments.py, `just comments`): a
# comment is a doc comment stating its item's contract; every other comment is banned,
# except a lone `// SAFETY: ...` over an `unsafe` block or `unsafe impl` and a bare ADR
# pointer (`// ADR-0051 §3`, nothing after it). A module joins with one `scan` line once
# the delete-comment skill has swept it clean; it never leaves. An entry (`<path> <n>`)
# would be a file of a listed module allowed n banned lines: it only goes down.
limit 0
test-limit 0
ext .rs
scan crates/sip-proxy
scan crates/sip-proxy-runner
